Ahh, yes, but how wonderful a game can be when the glowing potion is a potion
of object detection--probably the most common potion in the game, thanks to
nymphs, with no adverse effects when blessed and drunk, and not such a useful
potion that if the djinni pops out that you mind "losing" the effect of the 
potion in exchange for a wish (i.e., if it were a potion of gain level, you 
would probably still be happy for the wish, but at the same time you would lose
the effects of a heckuva nice potion).

Now for a related question with a possible spoiler...

Can you wish for 3 blessed glowing potions and get a djinni out of any (or all)
of them?  I don't know the probability of getting a djinni from a glowing
potion, but such freaks of chance could happen that you could get a djinni out
of more than one of them.  The dev team seems to have eliminated other ways of
getting wishes from wishes by making wands of wishing and magic lamps obtained
from wishes useless.  I was wondering if they had eliminated this possibility
too.
